{% block content %}
<section class="landing-hero">
  <div class="landing-hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Builder-first community hackathons</p>
    <h2>A reusable hackathon event operating system for communities that build in public.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Builder Season Playbook is a white-label playbook, template set, website, graphics package,
      and dashboard for running a 12-week community hackathon that produces real projects, not just demos.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="mailto:newman.gimbalabs+builderseason@gmail.com">Run Your Own Builder Season</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="https://nslanier.gumroad.com/l/tlmzp">Download the Playbook</a>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/dashboard/' | withBase }}">View Current Season Dashboard</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="workflow-panel" aria-label="Builder season operating snapshot">
    <div class="panel-header">
      <span>season-week-07.yml</span>
      <span>public</span>
    </div>
    <div class="status-row">
      <strong>18</strong>
      <span>tracked builders</span>
    </div>
    <div class="status-row">
      <strong>42</strong>
      <span>commits this week</span>
    </div>
    <div class="status-row">
      <strong>Sun</strong>
      <span>weekly update checkpoint</span>
    </div>
    <ol class="workflow-list">
      <li>Collect builder updates</li>
      <li>Review public evidence</li>
      <li>Publish the weekly signal</li>
      <li>Route users and feedback</li>
    </ol>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="landing-section split-section">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
    <h2>Most hackathons optimize for a final performance.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="problem-grid">
    <article>
      <h3>Demo theater</h3>
      <p>Teams rush toward presentation day while the deeper work stays hard to see.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Low follow-through</h3>
      <p>Projects disappear after judging because the operating cadence ends too soon.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Organizer burnout</h3>
      <p>Admins chase updates manually without shared systems for evidence, rhythm, or review.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Weak accountability</h3>
      <p>Communities cannot tell which builders are active, blocked, shipping, or learning from users.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section framework-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The framework</p>
    <h2>A builder-first operating rhythm pioneered by Gimbalabs Piece of Pie Hackathon 2026.</h2>
    <p>
      This reusable hackathon event operating system combines accountability, incentives, and open web
      tooling so builders keep moving, organizers keep the surface lightweight, and the community can
      inspect progress as it happens.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cadence-grid">
    <article>
      <span class="step-number">01</span>
      <h3>Long-form cadence</h3>
      <p>Run the season over weeks, not a weekend, so real projects have time to meet real constraints.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="step-number">02</span>
      <h3>Weekly updates</h3>
      <p>Use repeatable prompts, public posts, and lightweight check-ins to keep momentum visible.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="step-number">03</span>
      <h3>Evidence dashboard</h3>
      <p>Track GitHub activity, builder pages, project metadata, and manual review links in one place.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="step-number">04</span>
      <h3>User feedback loops</h3>
      <p>Move attention from judging to usage, conversation, iteration, and public learning.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

